 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/De71_3ShVsI/",
 "title": "Manifesting Through Audacious Goals and Identity Shift",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator explains that setting an audacious goal forces a new identity because the brain filters reality through those goals. By visualizing the best-case scenario and acting from that place while ignoring current circumstances, you can manifest your dream reality.",
 "key_points": [
  "Set an audacious goal so big that it forces you into a new identity.",
  "Step 1: Visualize 6 months to 1 year from now with everything coming true in the best possible case scenario.",
  "Step 2: Act from that place and focus on what is right in front of you.",
  "The creator shares that in 30 days she gained 300,000 followers and went from a broke, depressed student to living her dream life in 9 months.",
  "Step 3: Remind yourself of your desired reality daily and feel it.",
  "Step 4: Ignore your current circumstances and come back to the now.",
  "The creator notes that your current 3D circumstances need time to catch up to your inner reality and intentions."
 ],
 "content": "I filmed this last month and forgot to post it!! 💖 hi. You need an audacious goal so big that it forces you into a new identity. And this is how you're gonna do this, okay? Cause your brain filters all of your reality through the goals you set and the questions that you ask it. So visualize 6 months, 1 year from now, if everything were to go beyond your wildest dreams crazy. Like everything came true in the best possible case scenario. And then you need to release the belief that it has to be hard, because alignment is what is going to quantum leap you into that new timeline. You guys have seen it happen for me in real time. In 30 days, I gained 300,000 followers. I started this account 9 months ago. I went from a broke, confused, really depressed student to now I'm living the life of my dreams in my dream city doing work that I cannot even believe is possible. That is because I started scripting every single day of my life and filtering my reality through the lens of crazy fucking goals that made no sense. Everyone in my reality was like, um, are you sure you're gonna do that? Are you sure you're gonna pull this off? That's all intentional. That's all part of the process because your current 3D circumstances need time to catch up to your inner reality and your intentions. When you're getting too lost, you're getting a little concerned, come back to that audacious goal and filter all of reality through that. Stop leaking your energy in things that you cannot control. And if you are on this journey, hi, you have found your people and I also have a bunch of free tools for you in my bio.",
